1.Explain the difference between frontend, backend, and full-stack development with
suitable real-world examples.
 Frontend Development: Builds the user interface using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
 Backend Development: Handles server logic, databases, and APIs using languages like Java or Python.
 Full-Stack Development: Works on both frontend and backend.
 Example: An online shopping website where users browse products (frontend), orders are processed (backend), and a full-stack developer manages both.

2. Create a simple diagram showing how the client-server model works in web architecture.
