 •	GitHub: Stores and shares projects online. 
 •	Live Server Extension: Automatically refreshes web pages during development. 

5. Explain what a web server is and give examples of commonly used servers.
  A web server is software or hardware that receives requests from web browsers and delivers web pages or application data using HTTP or HTTPS. Common web servers include Apache HTTP Server, Nginx, Microsoft IIS, and lite speed which host websites and web applications.

6. Define the roles of a frontend developer, backend developer, and database administrator
in a project.

 •	Frontend Developer: Designs and develops the user interface. 
 •	Backend Developer: Creates server-side logic, APIs, and manages application functionality. 
 •	Database Administrator (DBA): Designs, secures, maintains, and optimizes databases to ensure data storage, backup, and fast retrieval. 

8. Explain the difference between static and dynamic websites. Provide an example of
each.

 A static website displays the same content to every visitor and uses only HTML and CSS. Example: A personal portfolio website. A dynamic website generates content based on user interactions and databases. Example: Facebook, Amazon, or an online banking website.

